# The generated corpus (data/transcripts/ and data/corpus.db) is committed so
# a clone can query without generating or enriching anything. Only the
# working files under data/ that aren't part of the corpus stay ignored here;
# see scripts/generate_transcripts.py to build a corpus of your own.

# What the running service produces about itself — conversation checkpoints
# today, captured records and telemetry later. It is per-installation, it
# grows with use, and it is worth nothing to anyone else, which is exactly
# why it is a separate file from the corpus: sharing one would mean asking a
# question dirties a committed binary. Created on demand, so deleting it
# costs nothing but the threads it held. The -wal and -shm siblings are
# SQLite's, and appear while the service is running.
data/usage.db
data/usage.db-wal
data/usage.db-shm

# Model weights and the vector index built from them, both kept inside the
# project instead of a user's home directory. Rebuilt on demand; see
# corpus_query/models/hf_home.py and corpus_query/retrieval/index.py.
.cache/

